course: dictionary
lesson: 10216
title: Choosing a material: titanium
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A material is what something is made from, like wood, glass or metal. Scientists choose a material for a job by looking at its properties, which are the things it can do and how it behaves. Titanium is a good example: it is a metal that is strong but light, and it does not rust easily.
explain: The body accepts titanium well, so it is used in medicine. «Titanium is also used for hip replacements because the body accepts it well.» Doctors need a material that the body will not reject, and titanium is one of them.
explain: Context helps you work out what light means. «Aluminium is about a third as heavy as steel of the same size, and titanium is strong and light, so both are used for light bike frames.» Here the sentence compares weight, so light means not heavy. Light can also mean bright, but the clues show which meaning fits.
fact: Titanium is a metal. It is silver-grey, strong and light.
fact: Titanium is a chemical element with the symbol Ti and atomic number 22.
fact: Titanium does not rust easily, so it is used in planes, spacecraft, bicycles and glasses frames.
fact: Titanium is used for medical implants, such as artificial hips, dental implants and pins in broken bones.
fact: Titanium dioxide is a white powder. It is found in paint, toothpaste and sunscreen, and it is a different substance from the metal.
exercise: «Titanium is also used for hip replacements because the body accepts it well.» What does accepts mean here? | Makes it rust | Pays money for it | Throws it away | *Does not reject it
exercise: Which of these is titanium used for? | *Spacecraft | Garden soil | Wooden tables | Chocolate bars
exercise: «Aluminium is about a third as heavy as steel of the same size, and titanium is strong and light.» What does light mean in this sentence? | Bright and shining | Pale in colour | Dim and dark | *Not heavy
test: What kind of material is titanium? | *A metal | A wood | A plastic | A liquid
test: Why is titanium a good material for a bicycle frame? | *It is strong and light | It rusts quickly and is soft | It is made of sugar | It is heavy and easy to bend
exam: Why is titanium a good choice for hip replacements? | It rusts in the body | It is a white powder used in paint | *The body accepts it well and it does not rust easily | It is heavy and cheap
